 "note": "future_1sg is the perfective form used after θα (simple future) and να (the book's 'infinitive'); prepend θα/να. aorist_1sg holds only true simple-past (aorist) forms. Verbs with no aorist (είμαι, έχω, ξέρω) have aorist_1sg null, their only past in imperfect_1sg, and no_aorist true; no_perfective marks verbs whose θα form is the present stem (θα έχω). θέλω keeps the aorist θέλησα apart from the everyday imperfect ήθελα. Entries listed in the 3rd person (person '3sg': αρέσει, βρέχει, πρέπει, σημαίνει, υπάρχει, μπορεί) use *_3sg fields instead of *_1sg; impersonal true marks verbs with no 1st/2nd person use. Parentheses mark possible but less common forms. past_group is the book's Chapter 8 classification where it lists the verb; null means not classified there (B1/B2 verbs: predictable -σ- but unpredictable vowel, learn as irregular).",
